    <string name="settings_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_body">eikon works on your device. It has no account and no analytics, and its data is excluded from Android backups.\n\nYour photos are never copied: eikon keeps a local index with file details (name, date, size, folder) so the library opens instantly. Deleting the app deletes the index.</string>
    <string name="settings_storage_encrypted">The library database (the index, albums, edits, captions and what the analysis found) is encrypted on this phone with AES-256. Its key is held by the Android Keystore.</string>
    <string name="settings_storage_not_encrypted">The library database could not be encrypted (%1$s), so it is still stored unencrypted. eikon tries again every time it starts.</string>
    <string name="settings_storage_reset_title">Library database started over</string>
    <string name="settings_storage_reset">The key that protected the library database was lost, so eikon had to start a new one. Albums, edits, captions and names you had added are gone. Your photos are untouched, and the analysis will run again.</string>
    <string name="settings_storage_reset_ok">Got it</string>
